Call of Duty 2: Big Red One - Custom Engine @PROJECT_VERSION@
=========================================================

Our own engine implementation of Call of Duty 2: Big Red One for
@COD_BRO_README_SYSTEM@: the renderer, sound, script engine, game logic and menus are
rewritten as source code of our own. The game's maps, models, sounds and
mission scripts come from your own copy of the Xbox game; no game code or data
is included.

The whole single-player campaign is playable. Multiplayer works over System
Link (your local network); Xbox Live is not available.


Setup
-----

Start cod_bro_launcher. In Options, General, choose "Extract from a disc
dump..." and pick the dump of your game disc (an XISO or a full dump): the
launcher checks it against the known editions and extracts it into the assets
folder. Or copy an already extracted dump into the assets folder yourself; the
launcher checks that too.

Then set the options below and press Play. (cod_bro starts the game directly
with the saved settings.)


Texture packs
-------------

Optional sharper textures (4x) for the levels and the menus, and surface maps
for Enhanced Graphics: install them on the launcher's Data Files page, Texture
Packs tab. They download from GitHub (SmokeDoggy044/cod_bro_tex) and only work
with your own game files.


Requirements
------------

@COD_BRO_README_REQUIREMENTS@


Controls
--------

Gamepads use their Xbox layout. Keyboard and mouse:

  WASD           move                 mouse          look
  left mouse     fire                 right mouse    aim down sights
  Space          jump                 C / Ctrl       crouch, prone
  R              reload               F              use
  G              grenade              V / middle     melee
  left Shift     sprint               Q / E          lean
  wheel / 1      next weapon          Tab (hold)     objectives / scores
  Escape         pause                F10            free the mouse

Menus: point with the mouse and click (right click goes back, the wheel
moves), or arrow keys, Return selects, Backspace goes back. In a level, click
the window to capture the mouse; Alt+Tab or F10 frees it.


Multiplayer
-----------

Start it with the launcher's Multiplayer button, or from the game's own
Multiplayer menu item. Play System Link: one player picks Create Match, the
others Find Match. It works between PCs on the same local network and between
two copies of the game on one PC. Every PC needs the same System Link port
(launcher; default UDP 3074-3077), and a firewall has to let those ports
through on the local network.


Options
-------

The launcher saves its settings in @COD_BRO_README_SETTINGS@, next to
the saves. Every setting is also a command-line option of cod_bro, which then
wins over the file; @COD_BRO_README_HELP@ lists them.


Reporting a problem
-------------------

Every start writes log.txt next to settings.ini; the "Open log folder" button
on the launcher's Tech Support page opens that folder, and "Open save folder" the
saves. Attach log.txt to your report (copy it first: the next start replaces
it), plus the save folder if the problem depends on your progress.

For a low frame rate, tick "Measure performance" on the Tech Support page
before pressing Play and play to where it gets slow: the log then also says
where the time went.


